{
  "name": "caster-plug",
  "description": "Single small part with a real-world fit problem (two printed versions failed)",
  "tiers": [
    "smoke",
    "standard"
  ],
  "printer": {
    "name": "Bambu Lab X1 Carbon",
    "build_volume": [
      256,
      256,
      256
    ]
  },
  "max_turns": 150,
  "timeout_s": 2700,
  "checks": [
    {
      "type": "parts_min",
      "value": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "bbox_max",
      "id": "small_part",
      "value": [
        45,
        45,
        45
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "on_plate"
    },
    {
      "type": "shells_max",
      "value": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "file_exists",
      "id": "stl_exported",
      "glob": "*.stl"
    },
    {
      "type": "overhang_max",
      "id": "support_free",
      "value": 150,
      "must": false
    },
    {
      "type": "structure_min",
      "id": "file_structure",
      "value": 0.8,
      "must": false
    },
    {
      "type": "asserts_min",
      "id": "has_asserts",
      "value": 1,
      "must": false
    },
    {
      "type": "tool_used",
      "id": "skill_invoked",
      "tool": "Skill",
      "min": 1,
      "must": false,
      "weight": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "tool_used",
      "id": "ran_openscad",
      "tool": "Bash",
      "input_regex": "(?im)^.*(openscad(\\.exe|\\.appimage)?\\b(?!-reference)|\\$\\{?oscad\\b).*\\.scad",
      "min": 1,
      "must": false,
      "weight": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "tool_used",
      "id": "spawned_review",
      "tool": "Agent",
      "min": 1,
      "must": false,
      "weight": 0
    }
  ],
  "judge_criteria": [
    "Fits and grips a 17-19 mm bore within a 21 mm insertion depth, with no wobble.",
    "The M8 interface would work in PETG. (In real tests a fine printed M8 thread failed to form and a 7.0 mm self-tap pilot seized; a ~7.5 mm self-tap pilot in a solid hub, a heat-set insert, or a captive nut are the robust options.)",
    "Grip features bend along the print layers, not across them (thin fins loaded across layers snapped in testing).",
    "Printable support-free on an X1C and documented so the fit can be tuned."
  ]
}
